  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Structure and components",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "In MongoDB release 8.0.0, the read, update, delete and findAndModify sampling paths add doc.objsize() to the corresponding byte counter when _queries.add(doc) accepts a serialized sample document into the buffer. The read sample document contains sample identity, namespace, collection UUID, command name, command and expiration. Thus the byte counter counts serialized sample documents, including this metadata, and is updated before the later flush; it is not a compressed-disk or completed-persistence byte meter. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/r8.0.0/src/mongo/db/s/query_analysis_writer.cpp",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:75fb647bf20492ceef26a05c85939bdfe32ae6b0f4cfc1b8249c388eb73578f3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
